# The I/L's second job node: a wall of eight lightning bolts that marches
# across the screen, each bolt striking fifteen times for 860% at master.
#
# The eight are real, not scenery. GMS gives the wall two invisible attack
# objects -- one for the moving form, one for the locked -- and each carries
# the whole of `mobCount 12`, `attackCount 15` and `380+16x`, so an enemy the
# wall passes over takes all eight. 103,200% at master is the largest single
# PRESS in the game -- the holds land more over the seconds they run -- and its
# rate against the cooldown is Spear of Darkness's almost exactly: 2,580%/s
# against 2,589%/s.
#
# Twelve enemies is GMS's own mobCount and what this game's hitbox rule works
# out for itself from the bolt's 300x610 box -- floor(300/70) * (1 +
# floor(610/250)) = 12, the two agreeing exactly.
#
# `cast_interval_ms` is GMS's `subTime`: the bolts land one at a time on a
# 210ms beat rather than together, so each falls on what the one before it
# left standing. Nothing here has a position, so a wall that clears its twelve
# moving onto the next twelve is what marching across the screen comes to.
#
# Dropped: the recast that locks the wall in place, which needs somewhere for
# it to be; and the immunity to attack reflection, which nothing here has.
name: "Bolt Barrage"
description:
  "Summons a wall of lightning that pulses forward, electrocuting enemies in "
  "its path."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
tags: SKILL_TAG_LIGHTNING
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_ICE_LIGHTNING_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_STAFF
base_delay_ms: 660
cooldown_seconds: 40.0
max_enemies: 12
lines: 15
casts: 8
cast_interval_ms: 210
base { skill_pct: 3.96 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.16 }
